  "worked_solution": "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (6{t}^{2}-4{t}^{3})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{t}^{3}-{t}^{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(2)=-5.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5 & =2(2)^{3}-(2)^{4}+C \\\\ -5 & =16-16+C \\\\ C & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=2{t}^{3}-{t}^{4}-5.$",
